      "writtenOn": "2019-05-02T17:06:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of setting the wake mask, can we just assert and de-assert the wake line? Basically setting of wake mask and then setting the host event bit is achieving the same thing. In order to ensure that HANG_DETECT gets reported, you will have to add it to ALWAYS_REPORT mask.\n\nThat way, we don\u0027t have to set the wake mask in different places i.e. one on sleep state transition and over here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 276,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "18f3af75e0ca0f13ca5d4264016b349cc78f3a4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "863b75b5_2d867207",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 276,
      "author": {
        "id": 1260470
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-02T17:34:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could assert the line, delay for some amount of time (how much?) and then deassert the line. \n\nBut is that really cleaner? By manipulating the wake masks, I don\u0027t have to make a tradeoff of hanging the EC for some empirical amount of time that guarantees the AP will see the interrupt. This also honors the wake mask for s0ix, if for some reason the AP wanted to mask the hang detect interrupt. It also reuses the appropriate infrastructure for waking the AP via events, so if somehow that mechanism changed in future boards, I\u0027m not tied to a GPIO here.",
      "parentUuid": "a127d5fb_60b7d9dd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 276,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "18f3af75e0ca0f13ca5d4264016b349cc78f3a4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "05c1eddd_2a9a7479",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 276,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T02:46:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I could assert the line, delay for some amount of time (how much?) and then deassert the line. \n\nMinimum requirement would be 4us.\n\n\u003e But is that really cleaner? \n\nI don\u0027t think so. Both are equally hacky.\n\n\u003e By manipulating the wake masks, I don\u0027t have to make a tradeoff of hanging the EC for some empirical amount of time that guarantees the AP will see the interrupt. This also honors the wake mask for s0ix, if for some reason the AP wanted to mask the hang detect interrupt.\n\nCan we set only the HANG_DETECT mask in that case? Actually, I was thinking we can just get rid of the requirement of mainboards having to set this mask in coreboot. That is just yet another mask which can be easily missed.\n\n\u003e It also reuses the appropriate infrastructure for waking the AP via events, so if somehow that mechanism changed in future boards, I\u0027m not tied to a GPIO here.\n\nSG",
      "parentUuid": "863b75b5_2d867207",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 276,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "18f3af75e0ca0f13ca5d4264016b349cc78f3a4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "030d056e_4fb385ce",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 276,
      "author": {
        "id": 1260470
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T16:29:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "4us works now, but might not be sufficient on Future Lake.\n\nSure, we could only set hang detect. So I guess I\u0027d need to check if hang detect is in the s0ix wake mask, and if so, get the current wake mask and OR in hang detect. Is that what you had in mind? Otherwise it feels a little weird to just OR in hang detect even if it\u0027s not set in the s0ix wake mask. If the AP really wants it masked, I\u0027d like to continue to honor that.",
      "parentUuid": "05c1eddd_2a9a7479",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 276,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "18f3af75e0ca0f13ca5d4264016b349cc78f3a4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b527497_e5c25969",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 276,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T21:28:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually, I was thinking on the lines of not having the host to set this bit at all, but I see your point about host intentionally wanting to mask it out. Thinking out loud: What happens if hang detect is not set in wake mask, but EC hang detect logic is enabled. EC ends up setting the wake mask that was provided by host and set the hang detect host event bit. That will not wake the host up right away but it should anyways help wake the host when there is any kind of user event resulting in wake from other host event bits. Let\u0027s continue with this change to read out the wake mask and set it directly here.",
      "parentUuid": "030d056e_4fb385ce",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 274,
        "startChar": 18,
        "endLine": 276,
        "endChar": 11
      },
      "revId": "18f3af75e0ca0f13ca5d4264016b349cc78f3a4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
