    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "942aa042_ee2bd7c5",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 318,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T02:46:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any reason not to call lpc_set_host_event_mask() directly here just like it is done above but with 0?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 318,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "18f3af75e0ca0f13ca5d4264016b349cc78f3a4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1c599fc9_ca1da1b0",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 318,
      "author": {
        "id": 1260470
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T16:29:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, that would be equivalent to what we had today. I was trying to route into common logic so that if someone added some new feature to manipulate the wake mask on resume later, it would only be reset in one common place rather than two. Do you think it\u0027s better to just set it to 0 directly?",
      "parentUuid": "942aa042_ee2bd7c5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 318,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "18f3af75e0ca0f13ca5d4264016b349cc78f3a4e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "143bf8dd_f22ab3a2",
        "filename": "power/intel_x86.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 318,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-05-03T21:28:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, one reason that I was thinking about is: power_set_active_wake_mask() sets a deferred call by default to ensure power signals have stabilized before setting the wake mask. In this case, where s0ix_complete_resume is called based on host command to indicate exit from S0ix:\n1. Deferred call is not necessary since we already know that power signals have stabilized and host is up.\n2. Since deferred call has lowest priority and if host ends up sending a host command to indicate entry into suspend state before EC gets to the deferred call, then the wake mask being set to non-zero can be interpreted very differently causing other side-effects.",
      "parentUuid": "1c599fc9_ca1da1b0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 318,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 27
      },
